WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.640
Two metal plates face each
other across a narrow gap.

2
00:00:03.690 --> 00:00:07.570
Put charge on one, an equal and
opposite charge on the other,

3
00:00:07.620 --> 00:00:09.690
and a voltage appears between them.

4
00:00:09.740 --> 00:00:13.250
Capacitance is the charge
stored for every volt.

5
00:00:13.300 --> 00:00:17.050
Now build it again, twice
as big in every direction.

6
00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:19.100
How much more charge per volt?

7
00:00:19.150 --> 00:00:19.820
Twice?

8
00:00:19.870 --> 00:00:20.790
Four times?

9
00:00:20.840 --> 00:00:21.790
Eight?

10
00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:26.120
In this mission, you'll find the field
between the conductors with Gauss's law,

11
00:00:26.170 --> 00:00:28.480
then integrate it to get the voltage.

12
00:00:28.530 --> 00:00:31.250
Then you'll use that
recipe on parallel plates,

13
00:00:31.300 --> 00:00:34.430
concentric spheres and coaxial cylinders.

14
00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:39.630
Your mission: predict how much more charge
per volt the bigger capacitor stores.
